    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our premier efficiency score of 83.29. Facing a favorable 4.52 xERA matchup against Civale, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite park factor and wind-aided conditions that maximize his power profile, making him an anchor for the lineup. Following closely, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.41) draws a target-rich environment against Kochanowicz, with a strong 5.14 xERA matchup providing the highest SP advantage of the day. **Kyle Tucker** (75.75) also registers as a strong play; despite the looming presence of Spencer Strider, **Kyle Tucker** leverages an impressive 17% SP skill boost to remain a must-start, while **Jackson Merrill** (73.87) rounds out our elite offensive tier, buoyed by a consistent lead-off role and a positive platoon split.\n\nMid-tier value is anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (68.57) and **Andy Pages** (68.65), both of whom benefit from optimized order placement and favorable park configurations. The decision to bench **Brady House** (54.99) was particularly difficult; he hovered near the cutoff, but his slightly lower projected efficiency compared to **Coby Mayo** (58.42)\u2014whose power profile is amplified by the same park conditions affecting **Gunnar Henderson**\u2014ultimately left **Brady House** on the outside. We continue to monitor **Drake Baldwin**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Sam Antonacci**, as their spots remain contingent on official lineup postings. Caution is advised with **Liam Hicks** (43.41), whose dynamic platoon penalty against Lovelady keeps his score near the replacement floor; he is an active start, but keep a close watch on his defensive utility throughout the game to ensure he maintains his expected value.",
